@*
 * FILE ROLE: Comprehensive reference for all Razor directives: @model, @using,
 *            @inject, @functions, @inherits, @implements, @addTagHelper,
 *            @removeTagHelper, and @namespace.
 *
 * SECTIONS IN THIS FILE:
 *   1.  @model      — strongly-typed model declaration
 *   2.  @using      — namespace import in a view
 *   3.  @inject     — dependency injection into a view
 *   4.  @functions  — C# methods and properties local to the view
 *   5.  @inherits   — changing the base class of the compiled view
 *   6.  @implements — adding an interface to the compiled view
 *   7.  @addTagHelper / @removeTagHelper — Tag Helper assembly control
 *   8.  @namespace  — CLR namespace of the compiled view class
 *
 * This view has no @model because DemoController.Directives() passes no model.
 * ViewBag is used for the page title (contrast with typed Model.* in other views).
 *@

@*
 * SECTION 2: @using IN A VIEW
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * @using imports a namespace for this file only. Types already imported by
 * Views/_ViewImports.cshtml (ViewsRazorSyntax.Models, etc.) do not need
 * repeating here. Add only what this specific view needs.
 *@
@using System
@using System.Collections.Generic

@*
 * SECTION 3: @inject — DEPENDENCY INJECTION INTO A VIEW
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * @inject ServiceType PropertyName injects a registered service from the DI
 * container directly into the view as a typed property.
 *
 * SYNTAX:
 *   @inject IMyService MyService
 *   → Razor compiles to: [Inject] public IMyService MyService { get; set; }
 *     on the generated view class.
 *
 * USE CASES:
 *   • IStringLocalizer<T>  — localised strings without passing to ViewModel
 *   • IUrlHelper           — URL generation inside a view
 *   • Custom options        — reading IOptions<AppSettings> for feature flags
 *   • IAuthorizationService — checking permissions to conditionally render UI
 *
 * RULE: @inject is for reading/display logic only. Never perform writes or
 * complex operations in a view — that belongs in the controller or service.
 *
 * IUrlHelper is already available as Url in all views. This @inject line
 * is for illustration; the IWebHostEnvironment injection below is practical.
 *
 * Microsoft.AspNetCore.Hosting.IWebHostEnvironment is registered automatically
 * by WebApplication.CreateBuilder — no manual DI registration needed.
 *@
@inject Microsoft.AspNetCore.Hosting.IWebHostEnvironment HostEnv

@*
 * SECTION 4: @functions — LOCAL METHODS IN A VIEW
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * @functions { } declares C# methods, properties, and fields that are
 * compiled into the generated view class. They can be called from anywhere
 * in the view using standard C# syntax (or @MethodName() in Razor expressions).
 *
 * Useful for:
 *   • Formatting helpers called multiple times in the same view
 *   • Computed properties derived from ViewBag/Model
 *   • Small rendering helpers to keep the HTML markup clean
 *
 * WHEN TO USE @functions vs A PARTIAL VIEW vs A TAG HELPER:
 *   @functions   — view-private utility methods; short and simple
 *   Partial view — reusable HTML fragment shared across multiple views
 *   Tag Helper   — complex, testable server-side processing on HTML elements
 *
 * NOTE: Methods in @functions are not reachable from other views. For shared
 * logic extract it into a service and @inject it, or into a Tag Helper.
 *@
@functions {
    // Returns a CSS class based on the environment name
    string EnvBadgeClass(string env) =>
        env == "Production" ? "color:red; font-weight:bold"
        : env == "Development" ? "color:green"
        : "color:orange";

    // Formats a directive name for consistent display in the table below
    string DirectiveCell(string name) => $"@{name}";
}

<h1>@ViewBag.PageTitle</h1>

@*
 * SECTION 1: @model RECAP — THIS VIEW HAS NO @model
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * This view omits @model deliberately to illustrate the difference:
 *   With @model ArticleViewModel  → Model is ArticleViewModel (compile-time type)
 *   Without @model                → Model is dynamic (runtime binding, no IntelliSense)
 *
 * Using @Model.SomeProperty without @model compiles to a dynamic access;
 * a misspelled property throws a RuntimeBinderException at runtime, not a
 * compile error. Always prefer @model for any view with structured data.
 *@
<div class="card">
    <h2>1. @@model directive</h2>
    <p>This view has no <code>@@model</code> — data is accessed via <code>@ViewBag</code> only.</p>
    <p>Page title from ViewBag: <strong>@ViewBag.PageTitle</strong></p>
    <p>Compare with Index.cshtml which declares <code>@@model ArticleViewModel</code>
       and accesses <code>@Model.Title</code> with full compile-time checking.</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
    <h2>2. @@using</h2>
    <p>Imported at top of this file: <code>System</code>, <code>System.Collections.Generic</code>.</p>
    <p>Today via System.DateTime: <strong>@DateTime.Today.ToString("D")</strong></p>
</div>

<div class="card">
    <h2>3. @@inject — IWebHostEnvironment</h2>
    <p>
        Environment name (from injected IWebHostEnvironment):
        <strong style="@EnvBadgeClass(HostEnv.EnvironmentName)">@HostEnv.EnvironmentName</strong>
    </p>
    <p>Content root: <code>@HostEnv.ContentRootPath</code></p>
    <p style="font-size:.85rem; color:#6c757d;">
        HostEnv was injected via <code>@@inject IWebHostEnvironment HostEnv</code>
        at the top of this file — no controller pass-through needed.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="card">
    <h2>4. @@functions — Local Methods</h2>
    <p>The <code>EnvBadgeClass()</code> and <code>DirectiveCell()</code> methods above
       are declared in a <code>@@functions { }</code> block and called inline:</p>
    <p>Calling <code>DirectiveCell("model")</code> → <strong>@DirectiveCell("model")</strong></p>
</div>

@*
 * SECTION 5: @inherits
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * Every .cshtml file is compiled into a C# class that inherits from
 * RazorPage<TModel> (where TModel is the @model type, or dynamic if none).
 * RazorPage<T> provides: Html, Url, ViewBag, ViewData, TempData, User, Context.
 *
 * @inherits CustomBaseClass replaces RazorPage<T> with your own base class.
 * The base class must still derive from RazorPage<T>.
 *
 * USE CASE: Add custom helpers or properties to ALL views by putting them in
 * a shared base class, then @inherits it (or put @inherits in _ViewImports
 * so it applies everywhere automatically).
 *
 * EXAMPLE (not applied here — would require creating the base class):
 *   @inherits MyApp.Views.ApplicationRazorPage<TModel>
 *   public abstract class ApplicationRazorPage<T> : RazorPage<T>
 *   {
 *       public string AppVersion => "2.1.0";
 *   }
 *   Then every view can use @AppVersion without @inject.
 *@
<div class="card">
    <h2>5. @@inherits</h2>
    <p>Changes the base class of the compiled view from <code>RazorPage&lt;T&gt;</code> to a
       custom subclass. Use in <code>_ViewImports.cshtml</code> to apply to all views.</p>
    <pre>@@inherits MyApp.Views.AppBasePage&lt;TModel&gt;</pre>
    <p>This chapter does not apply @@inherits — it requires a custom base class
       (out of scope here). The pattern is in → 06. View Components &amp; Partial Views.</p>
</div>

@*
 * SECTION 6: @implements
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * @implements adds an interface to the generated view class.
 *
 * SYNTAX:
 *   @implements IDisposable
 *   Then define the interface members inside @functions { }.
 *
 * Rare in practice — most view logic should live in services or controllers.
 * The main documented use is implementing IDisposable when the view directly
 * holds an unmanaged resource (extremely uncommon).
 *@
<div class="card">
    <h2>6. @@implements</h2>
    <p>Adds an interface to the compiled view class. Uncommon — shown here for completeness.</p>
    <pre>@@implements IDisposable
@@functions {
    public void Dispose() { /* cleanup */ }
}</pre>
</div>

@*
 * SECTION 7: @addTagHelper / @removeTagHelper
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * These directives control which Tag Helper classes are active for the view.
 *
 * @addTagHelper *, Assembly
 *   Enables all Tag Helpers in the named assembly. The wildcard * selects every
 *   class in the assembly that derives from TagHelper. For Microsoft's built-in
 *   helpers the assembly is "Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers".
 *
 * @addTagHelper FullyQualified.ClassName, Assembly
 *   Enables only one specific Tag Helper class.
 *
 * @removeTagHelper *, Assembly
 *   Disables all Tag Helpers from the assembly (e.g. to override @addTagHelper
 *   from _ViewImports.cshtml for a specific folder/file).
 *
 * In this project @addTagHelper is in _ViewImports.cshtml — applied globally.
 * A per-folder _ViewImports could use @removeTagHelper to restrict specific views.
 *
 * PREVIEW → Full Tag Helper authoring and usage in 08. Tag Helpers
 *@
<div class="card">
    <h2>7. @@addTagHelper / @@removeTagHelper</h2>
    <p>Declared in <code>Views/_ViewImports.cshtml</code> for this chapter:</p>
    <pre>@@addTagHelper *, Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers</pre>
    <p>To disable in a specific sub-folder, create a
       <code>Views/Admin/_ViewImports.cshtml</code> containing:</p>
    <pre>@@removeTagHelper *, Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers</pre>
    <p>Full Tag Helper coverage → 08. Tag Helpers</p>
</div>

@*
 * SECTION 8: @namespace
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * By default, Razor compiles each .cshtml into a class whose CLR namespace is
 * derived from the view's path:
 *   Views/Demo/Index.cshtml → AspNetCore.Views_Demo_Index (internal name)
 *
 * @namespace ExplicitName overrides this to a specified CLR namespace.
 * This is rarely needed in application code but matters when:
 *   • You reference the compiled view class from C# (e.g. in unit tests).
 *   • You use @inherits with a base class in a specific namespace.
 *   • You are building a Razor Class Library (RCL) and need predictable names.
 *
 * In _ViewImports.cshtml, @namespace sets the root namespace for all views
 * beneath it — individual views can override with their own @namespace.
 *@
<div class="card">
    <h2>8. @@namespace</h2>
    <p>Overrides the CLR namespace of the compiled view class.</p>
    <pre>@@namespace ViewsRazorSyntax.Views</pre>
    <p>Most useful in Razor Class Libraries where the compiled view namespace
       must be predictable. Rarely needed in standard MVC applications.</p>
</div>

@*
 * DIRECTIVES QUICK REFERENCE
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *@
<div class="card" style="background:#f8f9fa;">
    <h2>Directives Quick Reference</h2>
    <table style="border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; font-size:.85rem;">
        <thead>
            <tr style="background:#dee2e6;">
                <th style="padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">Directive</th>
                <th style="padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">Purpose</th>
                <th style="padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">Allowed in _ViewImports?</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            @{
                var rows = new List<(string Dir, string Purpose, string Imports)>
                {
                    ("@model T",            "Declare strongly-typed model",              "Yes"),
                    ("@using Ns",           "Import a namespace",                        "Yes"),
                    ("@inject T Name",      "DI into view as a property",               "Yes"),
                    ("@functions { }",      "Local C# methods/properties",              "No"),
                    ("@inherits Base",      "Change view base class",                   "Yes"),
                    ("@implements IFace",   "Add interface to view class",              "No"),
                    ("@addTagHelper",       "Enable Tag Helpers from assembly",         "Yes"),
                    ("@removeTagHelper",    "Disable Tag Helpers",                      "Yes"),
                    ("@namespace Ns",       "Set CLR namespace of compiled view",       "Yes"),
                };
                bool alt = false;
            }
            @foreach (var (dir, purpose, imports) in rows)
            {
                <tr style="background: @(alt ? "#f8f9fa" : "#fff");">
                    <td style="padding:6px 10px; font-family:monospace;">@dir</td>
                    <td style="padding:6px 10px;">@purpose</td>
                    <td style="padding:6px 10px;">@imports</td>
                </tr>
                alt = !alt;
            }
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>
